I: This is the TLI interview TOPSY subject zero eight nine. Activity has been described. Here's your first photo. And your minute begins now.
S: Okay I would describe the photo as maybe mid nine nineteen hundreds. It seems as though there's some sort of ruckus or panic. And someone's being called away. I would describe it as almost a fleeing scene where the man's trying to run and the woman's trying to hold the man back. Other than that it is black and white. It's very straightforward.
I: Alright thank you. There's your minute. So you said it looked like a fleeing scene like the man was trying to get away from the woman.
S: Mhm.
I: Why do you think he's trying to get away from her?
S: Oh just from the way it's drawn. Does that make sense? So it looks like there's pressing.
I: Like she's pressing into him?
S: Yes. But it almost looks like he's trying to run the same time.
I: So like he's pulling away?
S: Yeah.
I: Okay perfect. We'll move on to the next photo. And your minute begins now.
S: I see a woman on the bridge is dark. It almost looks as though when eclipse is happening. There are men working on what appears to be a sawmill or a grain mill in the background. Oh my gosh. The way it's drawn, it almost looks like it's threaded. Everything's sharp and bold.
I: So there's your minute. What exactly did you mean by threaded?
S: Well I'm not sure if you've just the way the canvas lies.
I: Oh okay so sort of the the the pencil work of the photo.
S: Yeah yeah.
I: Okay perfect. Here's your third photo. And your minute begins now.
S: It it's a different scene, that's for sure. Looks like a european countryside, almost a vineyard, with a horse and a man, this a woman in this school, and a pregnant lady. And they look across the cleft side over water.
I: Anything else you can see?
S: No. Looks like it's done.
